-> [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.flashing|Install OpenWrt (generic explanation)]]

Before OpenWRT 19.07:

  - Follow [[common|common instructions]] on how to temporarily load OpenWrt over TFTP in RAM. You will need a DHCP and TFTP server.
  - Login to the web interface ''%%(http://192.168.1.1)%%'', and set a temporary root password.
  - Using SCP, copy the sysupgrade.bin file to /tmp on the device.
  - Connect to the device using SSH
  - Erase the "firmware" mtd partition using the "mtd" command. This will no longer be required once the device is officially supported.
  - Launch the installation using sysupgrade. The update must currently (as of OpenWrt 18.06.1) be forced because the device has not been added to the white list yet.\\ <code>sysupgrade -F /tmp/openwrt-18.06.1-ar71xx-mikrotik-rb-nor-flash-16M-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin</code>

As of OpenWRT 19.07:

  - Follow [[common|common instructions]] on how to temporarily load OpenWrt over TFTP in RAM. You will need a DHCP and TFTP server.
  - Login to the web interface ''%%(http://192.168.1.1)%%'', and set a temporary root password.
  - Launch the installation using the web interface and the "upgrade" file (System -> Backup/Flash Firmware -> Flash image) as if you were upgrading from one OpenWRT version to the next.




